<title>CHINA: China signs $120 mln cargo ship deal with Burma.</title>
<headline>China signs $120 mln cargo ship deal with Burma.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>China National Machinery and Equipment Import and Export Corp signed a $120 million deal on Monday to build two cargo vessels for a Burmese shipper, the Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The Chinese firm would make two 12,000-dead weight tonne cargo ships for Burma's state-run Myanmar Five Star Line, the agency said.</p>
<p>The vessels would be built by China's Xin'gang shipyard, it said but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
